          <caption>
            <p>Coronal Approach to the Craniofacial Skeleton. This surgical exposure grants access to the frontal sinus, naso-orbito-ethmoid region, zygomatic arches, orbital roofs, and anterior skull base. Structures at risk include the frontal branches of the facial nerve and the supraorbital and supratrochlear nerves. Contributed by MH Hohman, MD, FACS</p>
